{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.65,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C4"],
      "pins": ["C4.1", "C4.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C4-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C4 is a 0.1 uF capacitor (libsource Device:C) with pin 2 on GND and pin 1 on an unconnected net. Its footprint is an inductor footprint, not a capacitor footprint.",
      "expected": "A decoupling/bypass capacitor should have both terminals connected to the intended power and ground nodes, and its footprint should match a capacitor. The specification is silent about C4, so standard practice applies: a passive with one terminal floating is not a valid circuit connection.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C4\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C4-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"C4\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C4 unconnected-_C4-Pad1_ 0 0.1u"}
      ],
      "impact": "The capacitor is electrically absent; if it was intended as high-frequency decoupling, the associated rail may have more noise/EMI. The inductor footprint also indicates a possible assembly or sourcing mismatch.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U8"],
      "pins": ["U8.13", "U8.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The SKW92A pins named LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX- are both connected directly to the GND net.",
      "expected": "Ethernet PHY data pins should not be directly shorted to ground. The specification notes that the Ethernet jack is not wired and that the module's Ethernet PHY nets otherwise appear as separate/single-node nets; unused PHY pins should be left floating or explicitly configured as GPIO, not merged into GND unless intentionally disabled and repurposed.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the RJ45 jack J5's data pads ... all appear in the netlist as individually unconnected, while the LAN1_RX+/-, LAN1_TX+/- global labels used elsewhere resolve to single-node nets containing only U5 (SKW92A) pins"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the Ethernet PHY is enabled, shorting a differential transmit pair to ground can cause excessive current, heating, and PHY malfunction; it also prevents normal Ethernet operation.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show at least one clear deviation: C4 is a capacitor with one terminal left floating and a mismatched inductor footprint. A second, lower-confidence issue is that the SKW92A LAN3 TX pins are tied directly to GND, which is not consistent with the intended separate Ethernet PHY nets."
}

